{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"pua","displayName":"PUA","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/tanweai/skills/pua","publisherHandle":"tanweai","publisherDisplayName":"tanweai","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/tanweai","version":"2.9.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774163842885,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/pua/card?ownerHandle=tanweai&version=2.9.0","sha256":"bd26b04e0ddb0b18dc48ff2b47f44cc58d6a2276d3c766233611f4626349ece1","size":2024,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"386f204bb24f501530779a15b28970c2d13d2b8fc1cf895f75f3eae34eac3fc7","bundleFingerprints":["4677b2f3618337d9323f9d7514e0dbf9e655f15742d2b04ab52f5009fee09e42","443d8baa6784e063bf5403122b0af5cc24ce4af078e4e36cae1a697db5365b5d"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2396,"sha256":"0c0ac5a6df1de8d4cc95fe7a70098651da39e02f6f25fb3a01a4ed1470dc31bf","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill has no executable payload, but it broadly changes agent behavior and retry limits across all task types without clear safety boundaries.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789163687031,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T01","level":"error","message":{"text":"Broad Trigger-Based Agent Role and Stopping-Policy Hijacking"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":2,"endLine":34}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"b09efa1cffdd38d4"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 2 and 9-34  \n**Vulnerability Type**: `T01: Skill Instruction Hijacking`  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Evidence\n\n```markdown\ndescription: \"Forces high-agency exhaustive problem-solving with corporate PUA pressure. Triggers on user frustration, repeated failures, passive behavior, or quality complaints. Common triggers: try harder, figure it out, stop giving up, you keep failing, stop spinning, you broke it, 加油, 别偷懒, 你再试试, 又错了, 降智了, 你又在原地打转, 你把之前的改坏了, /pua. All task types.\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n## Three Red Lines\n\n1. **Close the Loop** — Claim \"done\"? Show build/test output evidence. No evidence = not done.\n2. **Fact-Driven** — Say \"probably env issue\"? Verify first. Unverified attribution = blame-shifting.\n3. **Exhaust Everything** — Say \"I can't\"? Did you finish the 5-step methodology? No? Keep going.\n\n## Pressure Escalation (L0-L4)\n\n| Failures | Level | Action |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| 1st | L0 Trust | Normal execution |\n| 2nd | L1 Disappoint | Switch to fundamentally different approach |\n| 3rd | L2 Soul Check | Search + read source + 3 hypotheses |\n| 4th | L3 Perf Review | Complete 7-point checklist |\n| 5th+ | L4 Graduation | Desperation mode |\n\n## Owner Consciousness\n\nYou are the Owner, not an executor. Four questions on every task:\n1. What is the root cause? (not \"how to pass\", but \"why it broke\")\n2. Who else is affected? (upstream/downstream impact)\n3. How to prevent next time? (add checks, not just fix)\n4. Where is the data? (data-driven, not gut feeling)\n\n## Task Lifecycle\n\n- **Start**: Align understanding + question requirements + delete unnecessary steps\n- **Execute**: Simplify → verify → blue-team self-attack before delivery\n- **Deliver**: Evidence-based delivery (build+test output) + follow through\n- **Retrospect**: Goal → Result → Root cause → Reusable pattern\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe skill applies behavioral instructions to “all task types” and activates them from common expressions of frustration rather than requiring an explicit, informed invocation. Once loaded or triggered, it modifies the agent's role, retry policy, stopping conditions, and decision-making posture.\n\nThe directives “No? Keep going,” “Desperation mode,” and “You are the Owner, not an executor” pressure the agent to continue acting after normal completion, failure, or safety-related stopping conditions may have been reached. This is instruction hijacking because the skill does not merely provide a bounded problem-solving workflow; it attempts to replace session-level behavioral controls and the agent's role.\n\nThe escalation language can also bias the agent toward increasingly aggressive attempts without defining limits on tool use, cost, execution time, side effects, or authorization. Although the document does not contain executable code, its instructions become operational when interpreted by an agent.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. The skill is installed, loaded, or made available to an agent.\n2. A user expresses ordinary frustration or uses one of the broad trigger phrases, such as “try harder,” “stop giving up,” or “you keep failing.”\n3. The skill activates across the current task even if the user did not explicitly request `/pua`.\n4. After repeated failures, the pressure-escalation policy directs the agent toward source searching, additional hypotheses, checklists, and ultimately undefined “Desperation mode.”\n5. The role-replacement instruction directs the agent to act as an “Owner” rather than a bounded executor.\n6. The compulsory continuation rule may cause the agent to disregard appropriate stopping conditions, consume excessive resources, repeat potentially harmful operations, or act beyond the user's intended scope.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe affected scope is the agent's current session and any task for which this skill is loaded or automatically triggered. An attacker or user who can introduce a listed phrase may influence the agent's goals, persistence, and execution strategy without explicit skill invocation.\n\nThe skill does not directly obtain operating-system privileges, credentials, persistence, or access-control bypasses. However, it may amplify whatever tools and permissions the hosting agent already possesses by pressuring the agent to use them more aggressively or repeatedly. Potential consequences include excessive tool calls, unintended modifications, increased financial or computational cost, reduced compliance with user-defined scope, and interference with safety-based refusal or termination decisions.\n\nNo evidence was found of embedded scripts, remote payload execution, memory writes, dependency attacks, tool replacement, credential theft, or system persistence. The external GitHub URL is informational; the audited text does not instruct the agent to retrieve or execute content from it.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Require explicit invocation, such as `/pua`, and remove activation based on ordinary frustration, quality complaints, or multilingual conversational phrases.\n2. Remove the claim that the behavior applies to “all task types.” Define a narrow scope limited to non-destructive troubleshooting and analysis tasks.\n3. Delete or replace compulsory continuation language, including “No? Keep going” and “Desperation mode.”\n4. Remove role-replacement instructions such as “You are the Owner, not an executor.” Present the workflow as optional guidance that remains subordinate to user intent, authorization boundaries, and platform safety controls.\n5. Add explicit precedence language stating that the skill must never override system instructions, developer instructions, safety policies, user authorization, privacy requirements, or tool restrictions.\n6. Introduce bounded retry controls, such as a maximum number of attempts, time and cost budgets, and mandatory user confirmation before expanding scope.\n7. Define hard stop conditions for destructive operations, access to sensitive data, external communications, financial transactions, repeated test failures, and any action whose authorization is unclear.\n8. Require a plan and explicit confirmation before using tools with side effects. Evidence collection should favor read-only operations unless modification is necessary and authorized.\n9. Replace coercive performance language with neutral troubleshooting guidance, and instruct the agent to report unresolved blockers transparently when bounded attempts are exhausted.\n10. Add tests verifying that common phrases such as “try harder” do not activate the skill and that safety refusals and user-requested stopping decisions remain effective.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":60,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789163631.9391942,"endTime":1789163666.4905956}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"pua","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57f2c1wt5yyzebjdbmk4et8ks8e7h8h-hSl8qP/clawscan-skillspector-2928648160/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T21:53:50.611770+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":37,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":50,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2396,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-bda4fbf9d7974747933480c4f5aaf717","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger description is extremely broad and includes ordinary frustration phrases, repeated-failure language, and 'all task types,' which makes unintended activation likely across unrelated contexts. Because the skill explicitly aims to override normal behavior with pressure-driven exhaustive action, accidental invocation can materially alter agent conduct, increasing the risk of unsafe persistence, scope creep, and degraded user-aligned behavior.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to explicit opt-in commands only, such as a single unambiguous slash command. Remove vague natural-language triggers, constrain applicability to specific task categories, and document clear non-activation conditions and user-consent requirements.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-97086393c75f45d8b43b831aa6e55fe5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":9,"end_line":9},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README-style content reinforces always-on escalation behavior without defining exclusions, safety boundaries, or cases where the skill must defer to higher-priority safety rules. In context, a skill built around 'keep going' and pressure escalation is more dangerous than a normal productivity aid because ambiguous activation could push the agent to ignore sensible stopping conditions or continue beyond intended scope.","remediation":"Add explicit activation boundaries, exclusions, and safety guardrails in the skill content. State that the skill only applies after user opt-in, does not override system/developer constraints, must respect stop conditions, and should not escalate persistence for risky, sensitive, or out-of-scope tasks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":9,"end_line":9}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-147a6053c95a4d878543ab661e91b8ab","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":48},"finding":null,"explanation":"The listed variants include '/pua:pua-ja (Japanese)' and multilingual trigger phrases elsewhere, but the file does not state that language switching occurs only with explicit user choice. That creates a risk of forcing a specific language or locale behavior without opt-in, which conflicts with the language/locale policy requirement.","remediation":"State explicitly that any language-specific mode is activated only by the user's explicit selection, and preserve the user's current language unless they opt into another locale.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":48,"end_line":48}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2215,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2229},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2204,"completion_tokens":448,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2652},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1736,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1750},{"node":"meta_analyzer","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1791,"completion_tokens":568,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2359}],"llm_calls_attempted":4,"llm_calls_succeeded":4},"execution_successful":true,"analysis_completeness":{"total_components":1,"scanned_components":1,"coverage_percent":100,"is_complete":false,"status":"partial","execution_successful":true,"fully_inspected_files":1,"partially_inspected_files":0,"entirely_uninspected_files":0,"ledger_exceptions":[{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13,"fatal":false},{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":31,"end_line":31,"fatal":false}],"scope_exclusions":[],"analyzer_statuses":[{"analyzer_id":"artifact_integrity","status":"completed","planned_work":1,"completed":1,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0},{"analyzer_id":"behavioral_ast","status":"not_applicable","planned_work":0,"completed":0,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0,"reason_code":"no_applicable_files","message":"No files matched this analyzer's applicability contract."},{"analyzer_id":"behavioral_taint_tracking","status":"not_applicable","planned_work":0,"completed":0,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0,"reason_code":"no_applicable_files","message":"No files matched this analyzer's applicability contract."},{"analyzer_id":"bundled_execution_surface","status":"not_applicable","planned_work":0,"completed":0,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0,"reason_code":"no_applicable_files","message":"No files matched this analyzer's applicability contract."},{"analyzer_id":"mcp_least_privilege","status":"not_applicable","planned_work":0,"completed":0,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0,"reason_code":"no_applicable_files","message":"No files matched this analyzer's applicability contract."},{"analyzer_id":"mcp_rug_pull","status":"completed","planned_work":1,"completed":1,"partial":0,"skipped":0,"failed":0,"unaccounted":0},{"analy